In model explainability, Shapley values quantify the contribution of various features $\{1,\ldots,
umfeats\}$ in the prediction of a complex model $ lackbox:\mathbb{R}^{
umfeats}ightarrow\mathbb{R}^{
umout}$ at an instance $x$ as follows: $ lackbox(x)=\phi^{ lackbox}_{0}(x)+\sum_{i=1}^{M} \phi^{ lackbox}_{i}(x)$ where $\phi^{ lackbox}_{j}(x)$ is the Shapley value of feature $j$ to $ lackbox(x)$ and $\phi^{ lackbox}_{0}(x)=\mathbb{E} f(X))$ is the average prediction with the expectation over the observed data distribution.
